    "lawCode": "Amd §5, Chap 672 of 1993",
    "lawSection": "Monroe County",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S5942\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act creating the Seymour public library district in\nthe towns of Sweden and Clarkson, New York including the Village of\nBrockport; and to amend chapter 672 of the laws of 1993 amending the\npublic authorities law relating to the construction and financing of\nfacilities for certain public libraries, in relation to including the\nSeymour public library district within the provisions of such chapter\nand providing for financing through the dormitory authority\n\nPURPOSE:\n\nTo create the Seymour public library district in the County of Monroe\nserving the Towns of Sweden and Clarkson, as well as the Village of\nBrockport.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 is the creation of the Seymour public library district in\nthe County of Monroe serving the Towns of Sweden and Clarkson, as well\nas the Village of Brockport.\n\nSection 2 allows for the election of the district and all the laws\nrelated to its creation. Allows for the election of nine trustees.\n\nSection 3 allows for the organization and structure.\n\nSection 4 allows the voters to set the budget and funding for the\nbudget. The initial budget shall be determined by a vote of the voters\nof the district. All future budgets that increase or decrease shall be\nsubmitted annually to the voters.\n\nSection 5 allows for the charter, commencement of operations and\ntransfer of property and employees. Section 6 allows for ad valorem\nlevy.\n\nSection 7 States that unless otherwise provided the education law\nrelating to libraries shall be applicable to the district.\n\nSection 8 deems the district a special district.\n\nSection 9 adds Seymour Public Library District in the County of Monroe\nto the list of public libraries under the public authorities law.\n\nSection 10 is the effective date.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation has been asked for by the current Seymour Library. As\nthe current district serves three various municipalities and it not a\nspecial library district, the administration of the library is\ncumbersome. For one example, should any of the three municipalities\nvote down the current budget (which is the same for all three\nmunicipalities) the budget fails, even if it passes in both other\nmunicipalities. This legislation simply seeks to add the Seymour\npublic library district to the list of those other special districts\ncurrently in existence.\n\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPACT ON THE STATE:\n\nNone.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nThis act shall take immediately.\n\n",
